@startuml scenario_bootstrap_a_curve_to_publication
' Scenario: a blueprint becomes a published curve.
' Source for doc/knowledge/demo/scenario_bootstrap_a_curve_to_publication.org.
' Regenerate with: plantuml -tpng <this file>

skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor "Henry Jones\nmaker, Trading" as Maker
participant "Curve screens\nweb + BFF" as Web
participant "ores.refdata\nblueprint + pillars" as Refdata
participant "Simulated IR feed" as Feed
participant "ores.marketdata" as Market
actor "Mark Reid\ndecider, Operations" as Decider
participant "ores.inbox" as Inbox

== The market publishes its quotes ==

Feed -> Feed: build each pillar as an oresmd datum
Feed -> Market: tick per pillar, at the datum URI
Market -> Market: create the party's series,\nstore each observation

== The maker authors the blueprint ==

Maker -> Web: Curve blueprints > Add
Web -> Refdata: put ir_curve_bootstrap_config\n(name, output series, currency, index tenor, role, conventions)
Refdata --> Web: the blueprint, version 1
Maker -> Web: Pillars > Add, one per pillar
Web -> Refdata: put ir_curve_bootstrap_pillar\n(start tenor, end tenor, curve role)
Refdata --> Web: the pillars in maturity order

== The maker checks the recipe ==

Maker -> Web: Check > Run the test
Web -> Market: compute_curve(config, as_of)
Market -> Refdata: read the config and its pillars
Market -> Market: compose the pillar's datum,\nread its observation at the as-of
Market -> Market: bootstrap engine
Market --> Web: points (point_id, date, discount_factor)
Web --> Maker: six checks, points, forwards, findings

== The maker asks for the publish ==

Maker -> Market: publish-curve <config> <as_of> (shell)
Market -> Market: read the subject from the config
Market -> Inbox: raise marketdata.curve_publish
Inbox --> Market: request, state waiting
Market -> Market: write the curve_publish detail
Market --> Maker: "Raised. The publish waits on the decision."

== The decider decides ==

Decider -> Web: Approvals > open the request
Web -> Inbox: queue, request and subject
Decider -> Web: Approve, with a comment
Web -> Inbox: decide_approval
Inbox --> Web: approved, not by the asker

== The maker publishes the approved set ==

Maker -> Market: publish-curve <config> <as_of> --approval_request_id <request>
Market -> Inbox: verdict: approved, same subject, unused
Inbox --> Market: publish may proceed
Market -> Market: compute, then write observations and lineage
Market -> Market: stamp the output series\n(candidate becomes a published curve)
Market -> Market: record the publication\nand send the notice
Market --> Maker: published_at, published_by

== The published set is read ==

Decider -> Web: Published sets tab, published list
Web -> Market: list_published_curves,\nget_published_curve_sets
Market --> Web: sets with publisher, as-of, points, state
@enduml
